#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# digit_count

#% text
# `digit_count(n, b, d)` gives how many times the digit `d` occurs among the base-`b` digits of the integer `n` (a list of digits gives a list of counts). `digit_count(n, b)` gives the counts of the digits 1, 2, ..., b - 1 and 0, and `digit_count(n)` those in base 10. `digit_count(n, b, d, len)` counts in the last `len` digits, with leading zeros when `n` has fewer.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
digit_count(2147, 2, 1)
#% output
#= 5

#% cell
digit_count(122000)
#% output
#= [1, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3]

#% cell
digit_count(242442422, 3, [1, 2])
#% output
#= [6, 7]

#% cell
digit_count(factorial(100))
#% output
#= [15, 19, 10, 10, 14, 19, 7, 14, 20, 30]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `integer_digits`, `digit_sum`
